{"id":"ai-how-models-work","title":"AI: how AI chat models work","subject":"AI prompting","label":"AI prompting","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":160,"duration":159.76,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":462,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":12.505},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":12.505,"end":47.495},{"id":"explain2","title":"Limits","start":47.495,"end":82.545},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":82.545,"end":102.595},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":102.595,"end":111.655},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":111.655,"end":115.385},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":115.385,"end":137.865},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":137.865,"end":159.76}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":6.02,"text":"Have you ever asked a chat assistant a question and got a smooth, confident answer that turned out to be wrong?","w":[0.54,0.7,0.86,1.14,1.48,1.58,1.84,2.26,2.32,2.8,2.92,3.12,3.24,4,4.58,4.88,5.06,5.34,5.48,5.58,5.7]},{"s":0,"a":6.47,"b":7.14,"text":"I'm Kora.","w":[6.58,6.74]},{"s":0,"a":7.44,"b":12.08,"text":"Today we look at how these models work, and why fluent words are not always true.","w":[7.48,7.88,8.02,8.22,8.32,8.48,8.7,9.12,10,10.16,10.46,10.8,11.1,11.24,11.46,11.78]},{"s":1,"a":12.93,"b":16.67,"text":"Chat assistants are built on large language models, or LLMs.","w":[12.98,13.28,13.76,13.9,14.2,14.34,14.7,15.08,15.58,15.88]},{"s":1,"a":16.97,"b":19.5,"text":"A model is trained on a huge amount of text.","w":[17.02,17.12,17.5,17.68,18.06,18.16,18.3,18.66,18.92,19.04]},{"s":1,"a":19.8,"b":24.68,"text":"During training, it learns patterns in language, such as which words tend to follow which.","w":[19.82,20.16,20.92,21.02,21.34,21.78,21.9,22.82,23.06,23.2,23.44,23.76,23.96,24.06,24.42]},{"s":1,"a":24.98,"b":28.43,"text":"When you ask something, the words you send are called the prompt.","w":[25,25.14,25.36,25.6,26.42,26.56,26.86,27.04,27.46,27.6,27.82,27.96]},{"s":1,"a":28.73,"b":33.51,"text":"The model does not read your mind. It produces its answer one small piece at a time.","w":[28.74,28.92,29.32,29.56,29.82,30.04,30.22,31.02,31.12,31.62,31.82,32.22,32.4,32.7,32.98,33.06,33.14]},{"s":1,"a":33.81,"b":37.9,"text":"Each piece is called a token. A token can be a word or part of a word.","w":[33.86,34.1,34.42,34.54,34.82,34.9,35.78,35.86,36.28,36.44,36.6,36.68,37.06,37.2,37.44,37.54,37.62]},{"s":1,"a":38.2,"b":43.48,"text":"At every step, it predicts what is likely to come next, based on the patterns it learned.","w":[38.28,38.52,38.8,39.54,39.68,40.16,40.32,40.46,40.82,40.94,41.18,41.94,42.26,42.36,42.48,42.96,43.06]},{"s":1,"a":43.78,"b":47.07,"text":"That is why it can write fluently about almost anything.","w":[43.8,44.12,44.28,44.66,44.74,44.92,45.2,45.8,46.12,46.62]},{"s":2,"a":47.92,"b":51.95,"text":"It does not look facts up in a database unless it has been given a search tool.","w":[47.98,48.08,48.32,48.56,48.84,49.2,49.34,49.44,49.52,50.26,50.62,50.7,50.84,51.02,51.28,51.36,51.68]},{"s":2,"a":52.25,"b":55.72,"text":"Instead, it generates text that fits the patterns it learned.","w":[52.3,53.18,53.3,53.78,54.14,54.36,54.64,54.76,55.22,55.32]},{"s":2,"a":56.02,"b":61.07,"text":"That is why it can state something false with total confidence. This is called a hallucination.","w":[56.04,56.24,56.38,56.64,56.72,56.92,57.22,57.6,57.94,58.14,58.46,59.64,59.86,59.98,60.26,60.34]},{"s":2,"a":61.37,"b":65.17,"text":"Its knowledge stops at a training cut-off date, unless it can search.","w":[61.37,61.59,62.13,62.46,62.62,62.73,63.22,63.65,63.98,64.36,64.52,64.74]},{"s":2,"a":65.47,"b":70.35,"text":"It remembers only what is in the current conversation, within a limit called the context window.","w":[65.52,65.64,66.22,66.48,66.66,66.8,66.9,67.02,67.32,68.42,68.72,68.82,69.14,69.36,69.48,69.96]},{"s":2,"a":70.65,"b":73.07,"text":"It can make arithmetic and counting mistakes.","w":[70.72,70.82,70.98,71.22,72,72.14,72.52]},{"s":2,"a":73.37,"b":76.5,"text":"And the same prompt can give different answers each time.","w":[73.42,73.54,73.7,74.06,74.5,74.7,74.98,75.4,75.94,76.18]},{"s":2,"a":76.8,"b":82.12,"text":"It is good at explaining, summarising, drafting, giving examples, translating and brainstorming.","w":[76.84,76.94,77.08,77.32,77.44,78.14,78.88,79.44,79.74,80.7,81.36,81.5]},{"s":3,"a":82.97,"b":85.64,"text":"Suppose you ask for a biography of a famous person.","w":[83.06,83.46,83.66,83.88,84.02,84.1,84.7,84.8,84.88,85.24]},{"s":3,"a":85.94,"b":89.8,"text":"The model has seen many texts about that person, so it is usually right.","w":[85.94,86.08,86.46,86.64,86.9,87.14,87.52,87.76,87.94,88.66,88.82,88.92,89.1,89.46]},{"s":3,"a":90.1,"b":92.97,"text":"Now ask for the biography of a little-known person.","w":[90.1,90.32,90.54,90.76,90.98,91.54,91.7,91.81,92.53]},{"s":3,"a":93.27,"b":98.19,"text":"The model may invent details that sound real, because it is filling in likely words.","w":[93.36,93.5,93.86,94.04,94.38,94.9,95.12,95.48,96.24,96.54,96.66,96.84,97.2,97.36,97.72]},{"s":3,"a":98.49,"b":102.17,"text":"It is not checking a hidden file. It is predicting the next token.","w":[98.54,98.64,98.8,99.04,99.4,99.48,99.72,100.64,100.74,100.88,101.36,101.5,101.78]},{"s":4,"a":103.02,"b":106.15,"text":"A model gives you a confident answer with a reference to a book.","w":[103.08,103.18,103.54,103.76,103.94,104.04,104.62,104.96,105.12,105.22,105.62,105.78,105.84]},{"s":4,"a":106.45,"b":108.74,"text":"Does the confidence prove the book exists?","w":[106.46,106.7,106.84,107.46,107.78,107.92,108.16]},{"s":4,"a":109.19,"b":111.23,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[109.24,109.56,109.86,110,110.28,110.68,110.88]},{"s":5,"a":112.08,"b":114.96,"text":"No. Fluent is not the same as true, so check it.","w":[112.14,112.56,112.96,113.08,113.26,113.38,113.6,113.72,114.4,114.62,114.88]},{"s":6,"a":115.81,"b":123.55,"text":"First mistake. Treating the model like a search engine or a calculator. Use it for language work, and verify facts and sums yourself.","w":[115.82,116.16,116.98,117.32,117.42,117.76,117.94,118.04,118.42,118.86,118.98,119.06,120.22,120.38,120.48,120.64,121.02,121.62,121.78,122.3,122.78,122.94,123.18]},{"s":6,"a":123.85,"b":129.87,"text":"Second mistake. Believing an answer because it sounds sure. Confidence is style, not proof.","w":[124.02,124.38,125.5,125.96,126.12,126.48,126.8,126.94,127.38,128.06,128.66,128.78,129.36,129.58]},{"s":6,"a":130.17,"b":137.44,"text":"Third mistake. Forgetting the cut-off date, or thinking it understands you like a person. It predicts text. It does not know you.","w":[130.17,130.51,131.01,131.62,131.85,132.3,132.63,132.8,133.3,133.47,134.14,134.36,134.64,134.76,135.2,135.37,135.87,136.21,136.38,136.66,136.88,137.16]},{"s":7,"a":138.29,"b":142.61,"text":"Remember that an LLM predicts tokens from patterns, using your prompt.","w":[138.34,138.76,138.92,139.22,139.86,140.28,140.7,140.9,141.78,142.02,142.22]},{"s":7,"a":142.91,"b":146.8,"text":"It does not look facts up unless it can search, and it can hallucinate.","w":[142.98,143.1,143.34,143.52,143.74,144.16,144.36,144.68,144.76,144.96,145.76,145.9,145.98,146.12]},{"s":7,"a":147.1,"b":151.02,"text":"Check facts, dates and sums, and remember the context window.","w":[147.18,147.52,148.16,148.58,148.74,149.68,149.82,150.2,150.32,150.78]},{"s":7,"a":151.32,"b":155.37,"text":"Top tip: treat the model as a drafting partner, not an oracle.","w":[151.38,151.68,152.4,152.66,152.78,153.14,153.28,153.36,153.82,154.62,154.84,154.96]},{"s":7,"a":155.67,"b":159.16,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and you will use AI wisely.","w":[155.68,155.94,156.48,156.64,157.5,157.62,157.72,158,158.32,158.66]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Asked a chat assistant and got a confident wrong answer?"},{"at":6.37,"kind":"text","text":"Today: how AI chat models work"},{"at":7.34,"kind":"text","text":"How models work; fluent words not always true"}]},{"at":12.68,"heading":"Core idea","items":[{"at":12.83,"kind":"term","text":"LLM","detail":"Large language model"},{"at":16.87,"kind":"text","text":"Trained on a huge amount of text"},{"at":19.7,"kind":"text","text":"Learns patterns: which words follow which"},{"at":24.88,"kind":"term","text":"Prompt","detail":"The words you send to the model"}]},{"at":28.48,"heading":"Predicting tokens","items":[{"at":28.63,"kind":"text","text":"Answer comes one small piece at a time"},{"at":33.71,"kind":"term","text":"Token","detail":"A word or part of a word"},{"at":38.1,"kind":"text","text":"Predicts likely next token from learned patterns"},{"at":43.68,"kind":"text","text":"Can write fluently about almost anything"}]},{"at":47.67,"heading":"Limits: facts","items":[{"at":47.82,"kind":"text","text":"No database lookup unless given a search tool"},{"at":52.15,"kind":"text","text":"Generates text that fits learned patterns"},{"at":55.92,"kind":"term","text":"Hallucination","detail":"False statement said with total confidence"},{"at":61.27,"kind":"text","text":"Knowledge stops at training cut-off unless it can search"}]},{"at":65.22,"heading":"More limits","items":[{"at":65.37,"kind":"term","text":"Context window","detail":"Limit on what it remembers in current conversation"},{"at":70.55,"kind":"text","text":"Can make arithmetic and counting mistakes"},{"at":73.27,"kind":"text","text":"Same prompt can give different answers each time"},{"at":76.7,"kind":"text","text":"Good at explaining, summarising, drafting, examples"}]},{"at":82.72,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":82.87,"kind":"text","text":"Ask for a biography of a famous person"},{"at":85.84,"kind":"text","text":"Many texts seen, so usually right"},{"at":90,"kind":"text","text":"Ask for a little-known person"},{"at":93.17,"kind":"text","text":"May invent details that sound real"},{"at":98.39,"kind":"text","text":"Not checking a hidden file; predicting next token"}]},{"at":102.59,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":102.59,"kind":"question","text":"A model gives a confident answer with a reference to a book. Does the confidence prove the book exists?"}]},{"at":111.83,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":111.98,"kind":"text","text":"No."},{"at":111.98,"kind":"text","text":"Fluent is not the same as true; check it."}]},{"at":115.56,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":115.71,"kind":"wrong","text":"Treating model like a search engine or calculator"},{"at":123.75,"kind":"wrong","text":"Believing an answer because it sounds sure"},{"at":130.07,"kind":"wrong","text":"Forgetting cut-off date; thinking it knows you"}]},{"at":138.04,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":138.19,"kind":"text","text":"LLM predicts tokens from patterns using your prompt"},{"at":142.81,"kind":"text","text":"No fact lookup unless it can search; can hallucinate"},{"at":147,"kind":"text","text":"Check facts, dates and sums; remember context window"},{"at":151.22,"kind":"tip","text":"Treat the model as a drafting partner, not an oracle"},{"at":155.57,"kind":"text","text":"Keep practising with Knowzone; use AI wisely"}]}],"check":{"at":111.48,"seconds":10,"question":"A model gives a confident answer with a reference to a book. Does the confidence prove the book exists?","answer":"No. Fluent is not the same as true, so check it."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}